sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2020-xenobots-10> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Designs first evolved on simulated land had bounding gaits that did not transfer to living organisms; adding first-order hydrodynamics and randomized phase offsets produced designs whose behaviour better matched the living systems, in contact with the ground for 93.3% of evaluation versus 52.7% on the first pass.";
    dc:type "simulation-result";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Adding hydrodynamics and random actuation made simulated gaits match living ones";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Kriegman S, Blackiston D, Levin M, Bongard J, “A scalable pipeline for designing reconfigurable organisms”, Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences of the United States of America (2020), doi:10.1073/pnas.1910837117; section “Materials and Methods › Evolutionary Design.”. Scope: Soft-body voxel simulations of Xenopus reconfigurable organisms"
}
